        {
          "id": 2494566745,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "I don't understand. What part of this change do you foresee changing the behaviour, and how?\n\nThis patch isn't intended to functionally change what the tap does. Absent other changes, the reset and finish routines will only be called at tshark exit, so their addition at this time is just \"good housekeeping.\" But it's important for them to have the ability to properly clean up after themselves, should the outcome of #20432 result in changes to how tshark manages the lifetime of command-line taps.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6020526,
            "username": "boolean263",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "David Perry",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/6020526/avatar.png?v=1788830706",
