      ],
      "title": "tap-iostat: add reset and finish routines",
      "message": "tap-iostat: add reset and finish routines\n\nMove code which freed the memory state of the tap out of `iostat_draw()`\nand into a new `iostat_finish()` routine. Add code to this routine which\nfrees the doubly-linked list of stat items, which was previously leaked.\n\nAdd `iostat_reset()` function to reset all statistics when a new file is\nloaded. Both this and `iostat_finish()` are only registered as callbacks\nwhen registering the first iostat tap, to match that `iostat_draw()` was\nalso only registered once in this same way.\n\nMove `last_relative_time` from a static global to the per-instance tap\ndata.\n\nPing #20432\n",
      "author_name": "David Perry",
      "author_email": "boolean263@protonmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2025-05-06T14:34:48.000-04:00",
      "committer_name": "John Thacker",
      "committer_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2025-05-13T21:21:32.000+00:00",
